ral  America and we're enthusiastically  bringing support material support to  some of these regimes Walmart itself had  no direct connection there but what  disappears in a sort of story of young  people coming to the u.s. learning  business Christian values bringing them  home is how necessary the literal  physical extermination that strong the  part about Guatemala where the whole  sort of progressive intellectual class  and students are wiped out but people  who believed in liberal shopping  the grass yeah you don't have to win the  argument you kill the people  dump their bodies at the leftist  universities and there's a vacuum and  into that vacuum people who've been  trained in a very different model and  who has personal experience of the the  chaos and misery of these war-torn  countries in the 80s can step up and say  here's an alternative and and many of  these people work very hard to spread  the the values in the model that they  learned and of course now Walmart has  expanded into Central America the  Central American Free Trade Agreement is  part of the picture so it's important to  recognize what's necessary for this  economic vision to win out is frequently  terrorism you know but there's no other  word for it and covered action I will  say that you had quite quite astounding  evidence in the book so I was persuaded  I'm gonna jump in here and say that I  know we only have a few more minutes and  I wanted to ask you about this because  my own home city of Chicago was one of  the places where there was a big huge  fire a few years back about the siting  of a wall Walmart stores two stores  actually in Chicago and there was a big  local protest on the part of people who  thought that this was going to drive out  local businesses that was going to lower  wages in depressed wages in the city and  on the other side there were people  saying look these are stores coming into  poor communities bringing you know right  bargain prices that hard-pressed  fami